<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29189" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĭnūtal</span></b> ,
		ālis, n.
		minutus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A dish of minced meat</i> (post-Aug.), <i><span class="en">Juv. 14,
				129</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 11, 31,
			11</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In gen.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĭnū-tālĭa</span></b> ,
				ĭum, <i>petty</i> or <i>paltry things, trifles</i> (post-class.),
					<i><span class="en">Tert. Hab. Mul. 6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">culices, formicae, tineae et hoc genus
					minutalia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Anim. 32</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
